IMPORT prelude

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (Western Australia) -- planning for one's own incapacity, and being made the
-- subject of a guardianship or administration order.
--
-- SEAT: the adult planning for incapacity -- the donor of an enduring power of attorney (Part 9), the appointor of an
-- enduring guardian (Part 9A), the maker of an advance health directive (Part 9B) -- and the person for whom a guardian or
-- administrator may be appointed (ss 4, 43, 64). Every question is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (definitions used: mental disability, treatment, treatment decision, enduring guardian); s 4(3), (4)
-- (presumption of capacity; the less restrictive alternative); s 43(1), (2a), (2c) (guardianship order); s 45 (a plenary
-- guardian's functions and limits, borrowed by s 110G); s 53(a), s 54 (joint guardians, applied by s 110H); s 64(1)
-- (administration order); Part 9: ss 104, 104B, 104C, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109(1)(c), (2); Part 9A: ss 110B-110H, 110N;
-- Part 9B: ss 110P-110T; Part 9C: s 110ZD (the person responsible); Part 9D: s 110ZJ (order of priority for treatment);
-- s 119 (order of priority for other personal matters); Schedule 3 Forms 1 and 2.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49107, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49107.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with the
-- Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Amendment (Sex or Gender Changes) Act 2024 Pt 4 Div 9 (in force 30 May 2025). The
-- uncommenced ss 110RA and 110ZAA-110ZAC are not encoded.
-- Regulations used: Guardianship and Administration Regulations 2005, consolidated version 01-d0-00 (currency from
-- 5 April 2024, retrieved 19 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../../guardianship-and-administration-regulations-2005/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_46980.txt: reg 6 and Schedule 1
-- (the enduring power of guardianship form), reg 7 and Schedule 2 (the advance health directive form), reg 8 (notes are not
-- part of a form), reg 9 (the 2022 transitional period for the directive form).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Tribunal and its procedure, appeals and reviews (Parts 3-4, 7); a limited guardian's functions (s 46) and
-- an administrator's functions (ss 69-83); sterilisation (Part 5 Division 3); the Public Advocate (Part 8); recognition of
-- interstate and foreign instruments (ss 104A, 110O, 110ZA) except as one flag for s 107(1)(c); the Tribunal's declarations
-- and directions (ss 110J-110M, 110V-110Z, 110ZF-110ZG) except where named; urgent treatment (Part 9D Subdivision 1) and
-- abortion (Part 9D Subdivision 3); medical research (Part 9E). Whether a person has "full legal capacity", is "unable to
-- make reasonable judgments", or a form is "substantially" the prescribed form, is a finding of fact the Act does not define:
-- each is an INPUT. A judgment the Act hands to the State Administrative Tribunal is an input phrased "the Tribunal is
-- satisfied ...", never guessed.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) -- planning for incapacity`

DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `an enduring power of attorney`
    `an enduring power of guardianship`
    `an advance health directive`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are given as year, month and day; an age is in completed years on the given day.
@export How old am I, in completed years, on a given day?
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you were born
      `birth month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month you were born (1-12)
      `birth day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month you were born
      `on year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the day in question
      `on month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month of the day in question
      `on day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month of the day in question
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How old am I` MEANS
    IF `on month` GREATER THAN `birth month` OR (`on month` EQUALS `birth month` AND `on day` AT LEAST `birth day`)
    THEN `on year` MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE `on year` MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

§§ `4(3) -- the presumption of capacity`

-- s 4(3): "Every person shall be presumed to be capable of -- (a) looking after his own health and safety; (b) making
-- reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to his person; (c) managing his own affairs; and (d) making reasonable
-- judgments in respect of matters relating to his estate, until the contrary is proved to the satisfaction of the State
-- Administrative Tribunal." The section states the principles the Tribunal observes in proceedings under the Act (s 4(1)).
@export Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs and making my own decisions (s 4(3))?
GIVEN `the Tribunal has been satisfied of the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contrary has been proved to the satisfaction of the State Administrative Tribunal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed capable` IF
    (NOT `the Tribunal has been satisfied of the contrary`)

§§ `43 -- can a guardian be appointed for me`

-- s 43(1): where the Tribunal "is satisfied that a person ... (a) has attained the age of 18 years; (b) is -- (i) incapable of
-- looking after his own health and safety; (ii) unable to make reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to his
-- person; or (iii) in need of oversight, care or control in the interests of his own health and safety or for the protection
-- of others; and (c) is in need of a guardian, the Tribunal may by order declare the person to be in need of a guardian".
-- s 43(2a): the same for a person who "has attained the age of 17 but not 18 years" and "will, when he attains the age of 18
-- years," meet (b) and (c); s 43(2c): that appointment "comes into operation on the day on which the person attains the age
-- of 18 years".
-- s 4(4): "A guardianship or administration order shall not be made if the needs of the person ... could, in the opinion of
-- the State Administrative Tribunal, be met by other means less restrictive of the person's freedom of decision and action."
-- For a 17-year-old the three limbs are read as what the Tribunal is satisfied will be so at 18.
-- INFERENCE (not decided here): an enduring guardian already appointed may be such a less restrictive means.
DECLARE GuardianshipOutcome IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me now`
    `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me from my 18th birthday`
    `the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for me`

@export Can the State Administrative Tribunal appoint a guardian for me (s 43)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable of looking after my own health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(i), as the Tribunal finds it (for a 17-year-old: will be, at 18)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am unable to make reasonable judgments about my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(ii), as the Tribunal finds it (for a 17-year-old: will be, at 18)
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I need oversight, care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(b)(iii): for your own health and safety or to protect others
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 43(1)(c)
      `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 4(4): for example, by an enduring guardian you have already appointed
GIVETH A GuardianshipOutcome
`Can a guardian be appointed for me` MEANS
    IF `my age` LESS THAN 17
        OR (NOT (`the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable of looking after my own health and safety`
                 OR `the Tribunal is satisfied I am unable to make reasonable judgments about my person`
                 OR `the Tribunal is satisfied I need oversight, care or control`))
        OR (NOT `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of a guardian`)
        OR `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means`
    THEN `the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for me`
    ELSE IF `my age` LESS THAN 18
         THEN `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me from my 18th birthday`
         ELSE `the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for me now`

§§ `64 -- can an administrator be appointed for my estate`

-- s 64(1): where the Tribunal "is satisfied that a person ... (a) is unable, by reason of a mental disability, to make
-- reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to all or any part of his estate; and (b) is in need of an administrator
-- of his estate, the Tribunal may by order declare the person to be in need of an administrator". s 3: "mental disability
-- includes an intellectual disability, a psychiatric condition, an acquired brain injury and dementia". s 4(4) applies.
-- s 64 states no minimum age (contrast s 43(1)(a)); s 77(4) refers to "any legal incapacity attaching to a represented person
-- by reason of infancy". So age is not an input here.
-- INFERENCE (not decided here): an enduring power of attorney in force may be a less restrictive means.
@export Can the State Administrative Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate (s 64)?
GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 64(1)(a): all or any part of your estate; a mental disability includes an intellectual disability, a psychiatric condition, an acquired brain injury and dementia
      `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 64(1)(b)
      `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 4(4): for example, by an enduring power of attorney already in force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an administrator be appointed for me` IF
        `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate`
    AND `the Tribunal is satisfied I am in need of an administrator`
    AND (NOT `the Tribunal thinks my needs could be met by less restrictive means`)

§ `Making the instruments`

§§ `104(1a), 110B, 110P -- may I make it`

-- s 104(1a): "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may create an enduring power of attorney."
-- s 110B: "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may make an enduring power of guardianship ..."
-- s 110P: "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may make an advance health directive containing
-- treatment decisions in respect of the person's future treatment."
-- The test is the same for all three. "Full legal capacity" is not defined in s 3; it is an input.
@export May I make an enduring power of attorney, an enduring power of guardianship or an advance health directive?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc Which of the three instruments you want to make
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have full legal capacity (not defined by the Act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make the instrument` IF
        `my age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `I have full legal capacity`

§§ `104C, 110D -- whom may I appoint`

-- s 104C: "A person is eligible to be appointed as a donee or substitute donee of an enduring power of attorney if the person has
-- reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity."
-- s 110D: "A person is eligible to be appointed under section 110B or 110C(1) if the person has reached 18 years of age and has full
-- legal capacity."
-- Part 9B appoints no-one: a directive contains the maker's own treatment decisions (s 110P). Nothing in ss 104C or 110D
-- excludes a spouse, a relative, or a person who will inherit.
@export May I appoint this person as my attorney or enduring guardian (ss 104C, 110D)?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc The instrument you would appoint them under
      `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The appointee's age in completed years
      `they have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appointee has full legal capacity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appoint this person` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `an advance health directive` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `their age` AT LEAST 18 AND `they have full legal capacity`

§§ `104, Schedule 3 -- making an enduring power of attorney`

-- s 104(1): created "by instrument -- (a) that is in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1 in Schedule 3; and (b) in which
-- the donor of the power declares that the power either -- (i) will continue in force notwithstanding his subsequent legal
-- incapacity; or (ii) will be in force only during any period when a declaration by the State Administrative Tribunal under section
-- 106 that the donor does not have legal capacity is in force."
-- Form 1, paragraph 4, prints both declarations with the marginal note "One of these paragraphs must be deleted".
-- s 104(2): "not effective ... unless -- (a) there are 2 attesting witnesses to the instrument -- (i) both of whom are authorised by
-- law to take declarations; or (ii) of whom -- (I) one is authorised by law to take declarations; and (II) the other has the
-- qualifications specified in subsection (3); and (b) the instrument has endorsed on it, or annexed to it, a statement of
-- acceptance in the form, or substantially in the form, of Form 2 in Schedule 3 executed by -- (i) the person or persons appointed
-- to be the donee of the power; and (ii) where applicable, the person or persons appointed to be the substitute donee".
-- s 104(3): the second kind of witness "must be a person -- (a) who has reached 18 years of age; and (b) who is not a person
-- appointed to be a donee or substitute donee of the power."
-- Unlike ss 110E and 110Q, s 104 says nothing of the witnesses signing in each other's presence. Form 1 says "SIGNED AS A DEED".
DECLARE DurationDeclared IS ONE OF
    `it continues despite my later incapacity`
    `it is in force only while a section 106 declaration is in force`
    `both paragraphs are left in`
    `neither paragraph is left in`

DECLARE AttorneyInstrument HAS
    `in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what paragraph 4 declares` IS A DurationDeclared
    `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `other witnesses aged 18 or more who are not a donee or substitute donee` IS A NUMBER
    `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every donee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substitute donee is appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every substitute donee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it makes one of the two declarations` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS     `what paragraph 4 declares` EQUALS `it continues despite my later incapacity`
              OR  `what paragraph 4 declares` EQUALS `it is in force only while a section 106 declaration is in force`
    `the attestation meets section 104(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS     `witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 2
              OR  (`witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 1 AND `other witnesses aged 18 or more who are not a donee or substitute donee` AT LEAST 1)

@export Is my enduring power of attorney validly created (s 104)?
GIVEN `my power` IS AN AttorneyInstrument @desc How the instrument was made and witnessed
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made it
      `I had full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` IF
        `May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of attorney` `my age` `I had full legal capacity`
    AND `my power`'s `in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1`
    AND `my power`'s `it makes one of the two declarations`
    AND `my power`'s `the attestation meets section 104(2)(a)`
    AND `my power`'s `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every donee`
    AND (    (NOT `my power`'s `a substitute donee is appointed`)
         OR  `my power`'s `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every substitute donee`)

§§ `104(1)(b), 104B, 105, 106 -- when my enduring power of attorney is in force`

-- s 105(1): "an enduring power of attorney that is in force is not affected by the subsequent legal incapacity of the donor".
-- s 106(2): the Tribunal may declare "that the donor does not have legal capacity and that the power of attorney is in force" if the
-- person "(a) is the donor of an enduring power of attorney referred to in section 104(1)(b)(ii); and (b) is unable, by reason of a
-- mental disability, to make reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to all or any part of his estate".
-- s 104B(2): "a substitute donee ... becomes the donee of the power only on, or during, the occurrence of events or circumstances
-- specified in the instrument."
-- INFERENCE: a power of the s 104(1)(b)(i) kind is in force from its creation, while the donor still has capacity -- the
-- declaration is that it "will continue in force", which presupposes it is already in force. The Act does not say so in terms.
DECLARE AttorneyKind IS ONE OF
    `a continuing power`
    `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration`

@export Is my enduring power of attorney in force now (ss 104(1)(b), 105, 106)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind @desc Which declaration your power makes
      `a section 106 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has declared under s 106 that you do not have legal capacity, and that declaration is in force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my enduring power of attorney in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a continuing power` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `a section 106 declaration is in force`

@export Can the Tribunal declare under s 106 that I do not have legal capacity, so that my power of attorney springs into force?
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind @desc Which declaration your power makes
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 106(2)(b): all or any part of your estate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Tribunal declare I lack legal capacity` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` THEN `the Tribunal is satisfied that because of a mental disability I cannot make reasonable judgments about my estate`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Has my substitute attorney become my attorney (s 104B(2))?
GIVEN `the events or circumstances my power specifies have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the events or circumstances in paragraph 1a of your power have happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my substitute attorney become my attorney` IF
    `the events or circumstances my power specifies have occurred`

§§ `107 -- what my attorney owes me`

-- s 107(1): the donee "(a) shall exercise his powers as attorney with reasonable diligence to protect the interests of the donor
-- and, if he fails to do so, he is liable to the donor for any loss occasioned by the failure; (b) shall keep and preserve accurate
-- records and accounts of all dealings and transactions made under the power; (c) subject to section 109(2), may not renounce a
-- power during any period of legal incapacity of the donor; and (d) shall, if the donee becomes bankrupt, report that bankruptcy
-- to the State Administrative Tribunal. Penalty applicable to paragraph (b): $2 000."
-- s 107(2): for a power recognised under s 104A(2), "subsection (1)(c) does not apply".
-- s 109(2)(a): the donee may apply for an order "revoking or varying the terms of an enduring power of attorney, appointing a
-- substitute donee ...". INFERENCE: such an order is the "subject to section 109(2)" release; and the Act does not stop a donee
-- renouncing while the donor has capacity.
@export What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records and accounts (s 107(1)(b)), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records` IS 2000

@export May my attorney give up (renounce) my enduring power of attorney (s 107(1)(c))?
GIVEN `I am legally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, at the time, under a legal incapacity
      `the Tribunal has made an order on my attorney's application under s 109(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has revoked or varied the power, or appointed a substitute, on your attorney's own application
      `my power is a recognised interstate or foreign power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power was made elsewhere and recognised by the Tribunal under s 104A(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my attorney renounce` IF
        (NOT `I am legally incapable`)
    OR  `the Tribunal has made an order on my attorney's application under s 109(2)`
    OR  `my power is a recognised interstate or foreign power`

§§ `108, 109 -- revoking my enduring power of attorney, and an administrator`

-- s 108(1): where the Tribunal makes an administration order (or an order under s 65 or 66) for the donor's estate, it "may revoke
-- or vary the power"; (1a): where "the continued operation of an enduring power of attorney would be inconsistent with the
-- functions of the administrator", it "shall revoke the power or vary it to remove the inconsistency".
-- s 108(2): "(a) the donee of the power is accountable to the administrator as if the administrator were the donor of the power;
-- and (b) the administrator has the same power to vary or revoke the power as the donor would have if he were of full legal
-- capacity." s 109(1)(c): on the application of a person with a proper interest, the Tribunal may make an order "revoking or
-- varying the terms of an enduring power of attorney".
-- The Act nowhere says in terms that a donor may revoke. s 108(2)(b) assumes it ("the same power to vary or revoke the power as the
-- donor would have if he were of full legal capacity"). INFERENCE: a donor with full legal capacity may revoke under the general
-- law that s 108(2)(b) assumes.
DECLARE Revocation IS ONE OF
    `I may revoke it myself`
    `my administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal`
    `only the Tribunal may revoke it`
    `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by me`
    `a treatment decision is revoked if I change my mind`

DECLARE AdministrationEffect IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal must revoke or vary my power to remove the inconsistency`
    `the Tribunal may revoke or vary my power, and my attorney answers to my administrator`

@export What happens to my enduring power of attorney if the Tribunal appoints an administrator for my estate (s 108)?
GIVEN `my power would be inconsistent with the administrator's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 108(1a): whether the power's continued operation would be inconsistent with what the administrator is to do
GIVETH AN AdministrationEffect
`What happens to my power if an administrator is appointed` MEANS
    IF `my power would be inconsistent with the administrator's functions`
    THEN `the Tribunal must revoke or vary my power to remove the inconsistency`
    ELSE `the Tribunal may revoke or vary my power, and my attorney answers to my administrator`

§§ `110E, Schedule 1 -- making an enduring power of guardianship`

-- s 110E(1): "not valid unless -- (a) it is in the form or substantially in the form prescribed by the regulations; and (b) it is
-- signed by the appointor or by another person in the presence of, and at the direction of, the appointor; and (c) the signature
-- ... is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (d) it is signed by the witnesses ... in the presence of -- (i) the appointor; and (ii) the
-- person who signed it at the appointor's direction (if applicable); and (iii) each other; and (e) it is signed by each person being
-- appointed as an enduring guardian or substitute enduring guardian (an appointee) to indicate the appointee's acceptance of the
-- appointment; and (f) the signature of the appointee is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (g) it is signed by the witnesses referred
-- to in paragraph (f) in the presence of the appointee and each other."
-- s 110E(2): the second kind of witness must have "reached 18 years of age" and not be "(i) the appointor; or (ii) the person who
-- signed the enduring power of guardianship at the appointor's direction (if applicable); or (iii) an appointee."
-- Reg 6: "The form prescribed for an enduring power of guardianship is the form in Schedule 1." Its notes add: "The appointor does
-- not have to be present when an appointee signs the acceptance", and "Different witnesses can witness each appointee's
-- signature" (reg 8: notes "are not part of the form").
DECLARE GuardianshipInstrument HAS
    `in the Schedule 1 form or substantially so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my signature: witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `my signature: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` IS A NUMBER
    `those witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by every appointee to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each acceptance: witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `each acceptance: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` IS A NUMBER
    `those witnesses signed in the appointee's presence and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my signature is witnessed as section 110E(1)(c) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS     `my signature: witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 2
              OR  (`my signature: witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 1 AND `my signature: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` AT LEAST 1)
    `each acceptance is witnessed as section 110E(1)(f) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS     `each acceptance: witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 2
              OR  (`each acceptance: witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 1 AND `each acceptance: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` AT LEAST 1)

@export Is my enduring power of guardianship valid (s 110E)?
GIVEN `my power` IS A GuardianshipInstrument @desc How the power was made, signed, accepted and witnessed
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made it
      `I had full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` IF
        `May I make the instrument` `an enduring power of guardianship` `my age` `I had full legal capacity`
    AND `my power`'s `in the Schedule 1 form or substantially so`
    AND `my power`'s `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction`
    AND `my power`'s `my signature is witnessed as section 110E(1)(c) requires`
    AND `my power`'s `those witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's`
    AND `my power`'s `signed by every appointee to accept`
    AND `my power`'s `each acceptance is witnessed as section 110E(1)(f) requires`
    AND `my power`'s `those witnesses signed in the appointee's presence and each other's`

§§ `110F, 110G, 45 -- when my enduring guardian may act, and what for`

-- s 110F: "An enduring power of guardianship has effect, subject to its terms, at any time the appointor is unable to make
-- reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to his or her person." s 110G(3): it "may limit the circumstances in which
-- the enduring guardian may act to the circumstances specified in the power."
@export May my enduring guardian act for me now (ss 110F, 110G(3))?
GIVEN `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about your own person
      `the circumstances my power limits it to exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If section 5 of your power limits when your guardian may act, whether those circumstances exist; answer yes if it sets no limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my enduring guardian act for me now` IF
        `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person`
    AND `the circumstances my power limits it to exist`

-- s 110G(1): an enduring guardian "has the same functions under section 45(1) and (2), and is subject to the same limitations under
-- sections 45(3), (3A), (4A) and (4), 110ZR and 110ZT, in relation to the appointor as a plenary guardian has". (2): the power "may
-- limit the functions ... to the functions specified in the power".
-- s 45(1): the functions "in respect of the person" of a parent with parental responsibility, "as if the represented person were a
-- child lacking in mature understanding, but a plenary guardian does not ... have the right to chastise or punish".
-- s 45(2): "(a) decide where the represented person is to live ...; (b) decide with whom ...; (c) decide whether the represented
-- person should work ...; (d) subject to subsections (3A) and (4A), make treatment decisions ...; (e) decide what education and
-- training ...; (f) decide with whom the represented person is to associate; (g) ... commence, conduct or settle any legal
-- proceedings ..., except proceedings relating to the estate ...; (h) ... defend or settle any legal proceedings taken against the
-- represented person, except proceedings relating to the estate".
-- s 45(3): "cannot ... (a) vote in any election; ... (c) consent ... to the adoption of a child ...; (da) consent, under section
-- 21(2)(d) of the Surrogacy Act 2008, to the making of a parentage order ...; (d) under the Marriage Act 1961 ... give consent in
-- relation to the marriage of a minor, sign a notice of intended marriage or take part in the solemnization of a marriage; (e) carry
-- out a function under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 Part 5A of the parent of a child." (3A): "cannot make
-- a decision in respect of the performance of an abortion". (4A)(b): "cannot consent to the sterilisation ... except in accordance
-- with Division 3". (4): "may not make a will or other testamentary disposition".
-- Schedule 1, section 4B, lists two functions beyond s 45(2): "(h) advocate for, and make decisions about, which support services I
-- should have access to; (i) seek and receive information on my behalf". INFERENCE: these rest on the general grant in s 45(1).
-- Schedule 1's note to section 4 says an enduring guardian cannot "make decisions about your property or estate".
DECLARE PersonalDecision IS ONE OF
    `where I live`
    `with whom I live`
    `whether and where I work`
    `a treatment decision other than about an abortion`
    `what education and training I receive`
    `with whom I associate`
    `bringing or defending legal proceedings for me not about my estate`
    `which support services I have access to`
    `seeking information about me`
    `bringing legal proceedings about my estate`
    `selling my house`
    `voting for me in an election`
    `consenting to an adoption`
    `consenting to a surrogacy parentage order`
    `signing a notice of intended marriage for me`
    `consenting to an abortion`
    `consenting to my sterilisation without the Tribunal`
    `making a will for me`
    `punishing me`

@export Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me (s 45)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision @desc The decision to be made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could a plenary guardian make this decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `where I live` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with whom I live` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `whether and where I work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a treatment decision other than about an abortion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `what education and training I receive` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with whom I associate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `bringing or defending legal proceedings for me not about my estate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `which support services I have access to` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `seeking information about me` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export May my enduring guardian make this decision for me (ss 110F, 110G, 45)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision @desc The decision to be made
      `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about your own person
      `my power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether sections 4B or 5 of your power leave this decision out
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my enduring guardian make this decision` IF
        `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about matters relating to my person`
    AND `Could a plenary guardian make this decision` `the decision`
    AND (NOT `my power limits the functions or circumstances so as to exclude it`)

§§ `110H, 53, 54 -- joint enduring guardians`

-- s 110H: ss 53(a) and 54 apply "as if they were a guardian and represented person"; (c) s 54 applies "subject to the terms of the
-- enduring power of guardianship". s 53(a): "a guardian shall not perform any function without the concurrence of the other guardian
-- or guardians". s 54: "the surviving guardian or guardians may act on the death of any guardian." Schedule 1, section 3B, lets the
-- appointor say "I do not want the surviving enduring guardian(s) to act."
@export Must my joint enduring guardians all agree before acting (ss 110H(b), 53(a))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my joint enduring guardians agree` IS TRUE

@export If one of my joint enduring guardians dies, may the survivors act (ss 110H(c), 54)?
GIVEN `my power says the survivors are not to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you kept section 3B of the form (surviving joint enduring guardians not to act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my surviving joint enduring guardians act` IF
    (NOT `my power says the survivors are not to act`)

§ `The advance health directive`

§§ `110P, 110Q, regs 7 and 9 -- making a valid directive`

-- Reg 7: "The form prescribed for an advance health directive is the form in Schedule 2." Reg 9: "commencement day means 4 August
-- 2022"; "transitional period means the period of 6 months beginning on commencement day"; "During the transitional period, each of
-- the following is the form prescribed ... (a) the form in Schedule 2; (b) the form in Schedule 2 of the former regulations."
-- So the transitional period runs from 4 August 2022 to 3 February 2023 inclusive. Before 4 August 2022 the former form was the
-- prescribed form (INFERENCE: from the definition of "former regulations" as the regulations "in force immediately before
-- commencement day"; the former form itself is not in the deposit).
DECLARE DirectiveForm IS ONE OF
    `the current Schedule 2 form`
    `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations`
    `some other form`

@export Was the form I used the prescribed advance health directive form on the day I made it (regs 7, 9)?
GIVEN `the form` IS A DirectiveForm @desc Which form you used
      `year made` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you made the directive
      `month made` IS A NUMBER @desc The month you made the directive
      `day made` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month you made the directive
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my directive form prescribed` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `the current Schedule 2 form` THEN `the date` AT LEAST 20220804
    WHEN `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` THEN `the date` AT MOST 20230203
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the date` MEANS `year made` TIMES 10000 PLUS `month made` TIMES 100 PLUS `day made`

-- s 110Q(1): "not valid unless -- (a) it is in the form or substantially in the form prescribed by the regulations; and (b) the maker
-- is encouraged to seek legal or medical advice; and (c) it is signed by its maker or by another person in the presence of, and at the
-- direction of, its maker; and (d) the signature ... is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (e) it is signed by the witnesses in the
-- presence of -- (i) its maker; and (ii) the person who signed it at its maker's direction (if applicable); and (iii) each other."
-- s 110Q(2): "Despite subsection (1)(b), the validity of an advance health directive is not affected by a failure to comply with
-- subsection (1)(b)."
-- s 110Q(3): the second kind of witness must have "reached 18 years of age" and not be "(i) the maker ...; or (ii) the person who
-- signed the directive at its maker's direction". A relative, a beneficiary, an enduring guardian or a treating doctor is not
-- excluded.
-- s 110P: a directive is one "containing treatment decisions". Schedule 2: "If you choose not to make any treatment decisions in Part
-- 4, then the document is not considered a valid Advance Health Directive". So at least one treatment decision is required.
DECLARE Directive HAS
    `in the prescribed form or substantially so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was encouraged to seek legal or medical advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `other adult witnesses who are not me or my signer` IS A NUMBER
    `the witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `treatment decisions it contains` IS A NUMBER
    `my signature is witnessed as section 110Q(1)(d) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
        MEANS     `witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 2
              OR  (`witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 1 AND `other adult witnesses who are not me or my signer` AT LEAST 1)

@export Is my advance health directive valid (ss 110P, 110Q)?
GIVEN `my directive` IS A Directive @desc How the directive was made, signed and witnessed
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when you made it
      `I had full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had full legal capacity when you made it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my advance health directive valid` IF
        `May I make the instrument` `an advance health directive` `my age` `I had full legal capacity`
    AND `my directive`'s `treatment decisions it contains` AT LEAST 1
    AND `my directive`'s `in the prescribed form or substantially so`
    AND `my directive`'s `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction`
    AND `my directive`'s `my signature is witnessed as section 110Q(1)(d) requires`
    AND `my directive`'s `the witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's`

-- s 110R: a treatment decision "is invalid if [it] -- (a) is not made voluntarily; or (b) is made as a result of inducement or
-- coercion", or if "at the time the directive is made, its maker does not understand -- (a) the nature of the treatment decision; or
-- (b) the consequences of making the treatment decision."
@export Is this treatment decision in my directive valid (s 110R)?
GIVEN `I made it voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the decision of your own free will
      `I made it because of inducement or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were induced or pressured into it
      `I understood its nature and consequences when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the directive, you understood what the decision was and what would follow from it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my treatment decision valid` IF
        `I made it voluntarily`
    AND (NOT `I made it because of inducement or coercion`)
    AND `I understood its nature and consequences when I made it`

§§ `110S, 110T -- when my directive operates, and revoking it`

-- s 110S(6): "Subject to section 110T, a treatment decision ... is taken to have been revoked if the maker of the directive has changed
-- his or her mind about the treatment decision since making the directive."
-- s 110T: not revoked, and no change of mind, "merely because the maker subsequently makes an enduring power of guardianship (whether
-- about the same matter as the treatment decision or a different matter)."
-- Schedule 2 offers the statement "In making this Advance Health Directive, I revoke all prior Advance Health Directives made by me."
-- INFERENCE: ticking it is a change of mind about every earlier treatment decision.
@export Is a treatment decision in my directive revoked (ss 110S(6), 110T)?
GIVEN `I have changed my mind about it since making the directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have changed your mind about the decision
      `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only evidence is that you later appointed an enduring guardian
      `I ticked the revocation statement in a later directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a later Schedule 2 directive of yours revokes all prior directives
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my treatment decision revoked` IF
        `I ticked the revocation statement in a later directive`
    OR  (`I have changed my mind about it since making the directive` AND (NOT `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship`))

-- s 110S(1): a treatment decision operates "(a) at any time the maker of the directive is unable to make reasonable judgments in
-- respect of that treatment; and (b) as if -- (i) the treatment decision had been made by the maker at that time; and (ii) the maker
-- were of full legal capacity." (2): "operates only in the circumstances specified in the directive." (3): it "does not operate if
-- circumstances exist or have arisen that -- (a) the maker of that directive would not have reasonably anticipated at the time of
-- making the directive; and (b) would have caused a reasonable person in the maker's position to have changed his or her mind".
-- s 110S(4): the matters to weigh under (3) include the maker's age when the directive was made and when it would operate, the time
-- between, and whether and when it was reviewed -- weighed by others, so asked here as two facts.
@export Does a treatment decision in my directive operate now (s 110S)?
GIVEN `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot, at the time, make reasonable judgments about this treatment
      `the circumstances are ones my directive specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made for circumstances like these
      `the circumstances are ones I would not reasonably have anticipated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110S(3)(a)
      `they would have made a reasonable person in my position change their mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110S(3)(b)
      `the decision is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision has been revoked (s 110S(6))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my treatment decision operate` IF
        `I am unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment`
    AND `the circumstances are ones my directive specifies`
    AND (NOT (`the circumstances are ones I would not reasonably have anticipated` AND `they would have made a reasonable person in my position change their mind`))
    AND (NOT `the decision is revoked`)

@export How can my enduring power of attorney, enduring power of guardianship or advance health directive be revoked?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument @desc Which instrument
      `I have full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now have full legal capacity
      `an administrator of my estate has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has appointed an administrator for your estate
GIVETH A Revocation
`How can my instrument be revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `an enduring power of attorney` THEN
        IF `I have full legal capacity` THEN `I may revoke it myself`
        ELSE IF `an administrator of my estate has been appointed` THEN `my administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal`
             ELSE `only the Tribunal may revoke it`
    WHEN `an enduring power of guardianship` THEN `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by me`
    OTHERWISE `a treatment decision is revoked if I change my mind`

§ `Who decides for me`

§§ `110ZD -- my person responsible`

-- s 110ZD(2): "The person responsible for the patient is the first in order of the persons listed in subsection (3) who -- (a) is of
-- full legal capacity; and (b) is reasonably available; and (c) is willing to make a treatment decision". (3): "(a) the patient's
-- spouse or de facto partner if that person -- (i) has reached 18 years of age; and (ii) is living with the patient; (b) the
-- patient's nearest relative who maintains a close personal relationship with the patient; (c) the person who -- (i) has reached 18
-- years of age; and (ii) is the primary provider of care and support (including emotional support) to the patient, but is not
-- remunerated for providing that care and support; (d) any other person who -- (i) has reached 18 years of age; and (ii) maintains a
-- close personal relationship with the patient."
-- s 110ZD(4): "the patient's nearest relative is the first in order of priority of the following relatives of the patient who has
-- reached 18 years of age -- (a) the spouse or de facto partner; (b) a child; (c) a parent; (d) a sibling." This list is shorter than
-- the s 3 definition of "nearest relative", which Part 9C displaces.
-- s 110ZD(6): a person "is not remunerated for providing care and support to the patient although the person receives a carer
-- payment or other benefit from the Commonwealth or a State or Territory for providing home care".
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `my spouse or de facto partner`
    `my child`
    `my parent`
    `my sibling`
    `no relative on the list`

@export Who is my nearest relative for my person responsible (s 110ZD(4))?
GIVEN `I have an adult spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or de facto partner aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a child aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent of yours is alive and aged 18 or more
      `I have an adult sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a brother or sister aged 18 or more
GIVETH A Relative
`Who is my nearest relative` MEANS
    IF `I have an adult spouse or de facto partner` THEN `my spouse or de facto partner`
    ELSE IF `I have an adult child` THEN `my child`
         ELSE IF `I have an adult parent` THEN `my parent`
              ELSE IF `I have an adult sibling` THEN `my sibling`
                   ELSE `no relative on the list`

@export Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer for my person responsible (s 110ZD(3)(c), (6))?
GIVEN `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your carer's age in completed years
      `they are my primary provider of care and support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Including emotional support
      `they are paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc A Commonwealth, State or Territory carer payment or benefit for home care does not count as pay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` IF
        `their age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `they are my primary provider of care and support`
    AND (NOT `they are paid for it other than by a government carer payment or benefit`)

DECLARE ResponsiblePerson IS ONE OF
    `my spouse or de facto partner who lives with me`
    `my nearest relative who is close to me`
    `my unpaid primary carer`
    `another adult who is close to me`
    `no person responsible`

-- Each input below means: that person exists, meets the description in s 110ZD(3), and is of full legal capacity, reasonably
-- available and willing (s 110ZD(2)).
@export Who is my person responsible for treatment decisions (s 110ZD)?
GIVEN `an adult spouse or partner living with me qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(a): aged 18 or more, living with you, capable, available and willing
      `my nearest relative is close to me and qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(b): frequent personal contact and a genuine interest in your welfare; capable, available and willing
      `my unpaid primary carer qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(c): capable, available and willing
      `another adult close to me qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZD(3)(d): capable, available and willing
GIVETH A ResponsiblePerson
`Who is my person responsible` MEANS
    IF `an adult spouse or partner living with me qualifies` THEN `my spouse or de facto partner who lives with me`
    ELSE IF `my nearest relative is close to me and qualifies` THEN `my nearest relative who is close to me`
         ELSE IF `my unpaid primary carer qualifies` THEN `my unpaid primary carer`
              ELSE IF `another adult close to me qualifies` THEN `another adult who is close to me`
                   ELSE `no person responsible`

§§ `110ZJ, 119 -- who decides, in order`

-- s 110ZJ(1): applies "if a patient is unable to make reasonable judgments in respect of any treatment proposed" (subject to the urgent
-- treatment Subdivision and s 110ZIB, not encoded). (2): "If the patient has made an advance health directive containing a treatment
-- decision in respect of the treatment, whether or not the treatment is provided ... must be decided in accordance with the treatment
-- decision." (3): if not, an enduring guardian who "(i) is authorised to make a treatment decision in respect of the treatment; and
-- (ii) is reasonably available; and (iii) is willing" decides; (4): if not, a guardian on the same terms; (5): if not, "the person
-- responsible for the patient under section 110ZD".
-- INFERENCE: (2) is read with s 110S, so a treatment decision that does not operate (or is revoked) does not take priority.
-- s 119: for a matter "relating to their person other than -- (a) treatment ...; or (b) medical research", the enduring guardian (if
-- authorised, reasonably available and willing) decides; if not, the guardian on the same terms. s 119 names no-one further.
DECLARE Decider IS ONE OF
    `I decide myself`
    `the treatment decision in my directive`
    `my enduring guardian`
    `my guardian`
    `my person responsible`
    `no-one under the section`

@export If treatment is proposed, who decides whether I get it (s 110ZJ)?
GIVEN `I can make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can decide for yourself
      `a treatment decision in my directive covers the treatment and operates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc See "Does a treatment decision in my directive operate now"
      `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(3)(b)
      `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 110ZJ(4)(b): a guardian appointed by the Tribunal
      `I have a person responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc See "Who is my person responsible"
GIVETH A Decider
`Who decides my treatment` MEANS
    IF `I can make reasonable judgments about the treatment` THEN `I decide myself`
    ELSE IF `a treatment decision in my directive covers the treatment and operates` THEN `the treatment decision in my directive`
         ELSE IF `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `my enduring guardian`
              ELSE IF `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `my guardian`
                   ELSE IF `I have a person responsible` THEN `my person responsible`
                        ELSE `no-one under the section`

@export For a personal matter other than treatment or medical research, who decides for me (s 119)?
GIVEN `I can make reasonable judgments about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can decide for yourself
      `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 119(2)
      `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 119(3): a guardian appointed by the Tribunal
GIVETH A Decider
`Who decides my other personal matters` MEANS
    IF `I can make reasonable judgments about the matter` THEN `I decide myself`
    ELSE IF `my enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `my enduring guardian`
         ELSE IF `my guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `my guardian`
              ELSE `no-one under the section`
